{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And He said:</b> The verse speaks in the manner that listeners will understand, for HaShem does not exert Himself in any of the creations. Now the meaning is: <i>You pitied a thing you did not make — how should I not pity my handiwork?!</i>" "<b>The word בן</b> — with a hirik, like בן נון. Now if the wicked son of the snake did not rejoice in the plant except for one day, from morning until evening — and behold it began growing from the start of the night until morning, and at evening it began to wither, and by the rise of dawn it was entirely dry — therefore he said: <i>that it was בן לילה</i> [of a night], <i>and בן לילה it perished.</i>"], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "הרשע והנה לא שמח read as one clause; 'son of the snake' translates בן הכות literally without resolving the idiom."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:16.525855763Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}